  triage:verifiedInRound "ttl-reconcile-ay-r1" ;
  triage:resolutionNote "Not a code fix -- closed as an accepted P-E(a)/A2 process deviation per Rand's ruling, relayed by fenix via team-lead message 01M1Y7MMHAFEKY8HBWRVKMPKV2. Ruling: the boundary TOML content itself is correct (already verified by boundary-guard in the original triage), and the commit-order deviation (boundary bundle landing as commit 9 of 19 rather than commit 1, per fenix's earlier author-timestamp/gh-stack-sync-force-push analysis) requires no history rewrite. Status set to 'closed' (not 'fixed') to reflect that this is a policy acceptance of the existing history, not a remediation of a defect. No content on feature/ay3-herdr-endpoint-doctor-config or integrate/phase-ay was changed as part of this closure." .

